Mark the host sub-libraries alwayslink for the shared build

cc_shared_library only whole-archives its direct dependencies. The seventeen
host sub-libraries are referenced only from Swift, so a lazy archive link
drops them. alwayslink keeps them.

The four cuda_library targets stay lazy. Their kernels are reached through
the registrant references in ccv_nnc_cmd.inc, and forcing them would add
hundreds of megabytes of kernels the binaries never contained. nnc_headers
stays lazy too, so co.c does not put a second copy of the coroutine TLS into
every consumer.

nnc_dynamic_headers exports the headers, defines and include paths that the
static ccv and nnc targets give their consumers, including the bare sqlite3.h
include path from @sqlite3 on Linux. It is the interface for s4nnc's
ccv_nnc_dynamic.
